c) The building shall be provided with a means to protect the lift(s) from the effects of fire and smoke at every landing, a safe area directly outside the lift door, and a fire-resistant structure;
d) The lift lobby at each floor shall be enclosed and separated from the remainder of the floor by a smoke barrier.  The lift lobby door shall be 2 h fire rated and shall close automatically upon initiation of building fire alarm. The lift lobby shall be large enough to accommodate at least 25 percent of the floor population at 0.28 m2 per person;
e) The lift lobbies and staircase shall be pressurized, if required;
f) The lift lobbies shall be provided with CCTV cameras with the monitor located in FCC/BMS room;
g) Fire/smoke/temperature detectors shall be provided in the building in a thoughtful manner in all areas of the building including lift shaft, machine room, lift lobbies, etc;
h) Activation of any of those detectors which signifies unsafe operating environment for the evacuation lift(s) shall initiate Phase I operation of the fireman‘s/non fireman‘s lift; and suspend the evacuation operation;
j) The fire alarm system may have a provision to automatically send public announcement messages to the residents of the floor with active alarm and to the residents of two upper and two lower contiguous floors;
k) Power supplies shall be secure and reliable; the provision of a secondary supply is essential.  The cable providing power to the lift(s) shall be fire protected to the same fire protection level as given to the lift well structure;
m) The secondary power supply shall be sufficient to run the evacuation lift at the rated load and rated speed for a minimum period equal to the planned evacuation time consistent with the evacuation strategy;
n) The car lighting shall be also supplied by secondary power supply;
p) The normal power feeders and backup power feeders shall be provided with 2 h fire resistance rated enclosures until they reach the machine room/controller;
q) The source of the secondary supply, the level of independence between the primary and secondary supplies;
r) The source of the secondary power supply and automatic switch gear shall be located in a fire protected area;
s) The building shall be designed to minimize the risk of flooding into the lift or lift well.  To this end sprinkler discharge, burst pipes, fire hose, etc should not be located to discharge towards the lift and any water close to the lift should be directed away from it by sloping floors, etc;
t) Water sensor shall be provided in the pit to shut down the lift in case the operation becomes unsafe due to accumulation of water in the pit;
u) Interior exit stairwell doors if locked, shall automatically unlock permitting exit and re-entry upon setting of alarm;
v) The lift shall be maintained, and the evacuation operation shall be tested at suitable regular intervals;
w) The building shall have a fire safety and evacuation plan including procedures for evacuation using stairs and lifts, the role of wardens, a routine training and drills for occupants;
y) Training shall include the message that lifts shall not be used for evacuation in buildings not having lifts provided with special occupant evacuation operation;
z) The machine room and lift lobbies shall be maintained with minimal fire load;
