12 LIFT ENQUIRY OR INVITATION TO TENDER
12.1 General
A period of two to four weeks is normally sufficient for return of tenders.  This should be extended, if large numbers of lifts or special requirements are involved.
The enquiry documents should be kept to the essential minimum, and should be strictly confined to material relevant to the lifts works and to the particular project concerned.
When enquiring for and ordering lifts, the particulars given below should be furnished:
a) Type of lift (passenger, goods, service or dumb waiter);
b) Number of lifts required;
c) Capacity/load of lift (s): number of persons (in kg);
d) Rated speed (m/s);
e) Travel (in m) and building height;
